WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.562
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:12.562 --> 00:00:18.862
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:18.862 --> 00:00:34.862
Old Maid: avoid the final joker
The 53-card deck includes one joker. Matching ranks are discarded automatically after dealing. Follow Demo N through all three deals.

00:00:34.862 --> 00:00:45.862
Click a neighbor’s card back
On your turn, click one card in the indicated neighbor’s face-down fan. You choose a position without seeing its face in advance.

00:00:45.862 --> 00:00:54.864
Draw clockwise from the next player who still has cards, skipping empty hands.

00:00:54.864 --> 00:01:06.964
Pairs are discarded automatically
Keep drawing and watch your own hand and public discarded pairs. A matching rank pairs automatically without a separate submission.

00:01:06.964 --> 00:01:16.864
Matching ranks pair regardless of suit. The joker has no partner, and an unpaired draw remains private.

00:01:16.864 --> 00:01:27.864
Hand order and hidden information
You can drag your own cards to reorder them. Draw by clicking a neighbor’s card back. The following repeated draws run faster.

00:01:27.864 --> 00:01:36.864
A card-back position does not guarantee a previously seen card remains there. Do not treat a position as a known face.

00:01:36.864 --> 00:01:48.964
Empty hands leave the deal
Speed through the closing draws. Watch empty-handed players get skipped while the remaining players continue.

00:01:48.964 --> 00:01:58.864
The deal ends with one joker holder. Four players score 3, 2, 1, and 0 by finishing order.

00:01:58.864 --> 00:02:14.863
One deal ends; totals carry forward
The first deal is complete and the log names Demo E as the joker holder. A fresh deal has started, with cumulative scores retained.

00:02:14.863 --> 00:02:50.863
Speed through deals two and three
Every remaining draw, automatic pair, exit, and fresh deal plays in order until all three deals finish normally.

00:02:50.863 --> 00:03:09.867
Old Maid: three-deal totals
Demo S wins with 7 points. Demo E and W each have 4, and N has 3.
